o  organisms for more than 6,000 years to  make useful food products such as bread  and cheese and to preserve dairy  products so what has our ability to read  and write DNA allowed us to do that is  fundamentally different now scientists  now envision using those four basic  building blocks of DNA to design entire  biological systems from the ground up  with as much precision as an engineer  can design a bridge think about it DNA  in its basic building blocks AGC team  hold the genetic code for every function  within an organism just like infinite  permutations of zeros and ones form the  basis for designing and writing software  code that drive all functions of  technology these nucleobases can be used  to write the genetic code for and build  entirely new biological systems from the  ground up the practice is called  synthetic biology or engineering biology  in the most recent vernacular the coming  revolution in engineering biology will  transform the industries of energy  agriculture health care chemicals and  bioremediation to name just a few and it  will also raise social and ethical  questions including what constitutes  life and what it means  Uman as well as important security  concerns about biosafety and by our  terrorism synthetic biology bridges a  number of scientific disciplines such as  metabolic engineering molecular biology  microbiology systems biology synthetic  chemistry chemical engineering and  genetic engineering it also relies on a  constellation of supporting technologies  like DNA sequencing and synthesis  laboratory automation design and  modeling software bioinformatics and big  data and computing in theory how does  all this work together to make biology  engineer abell scientists must construct  predictable systems and standardized  parts to do this they use computer  software to write the code that design  organisms in the abstract and predict  their production ideally you want to  design build test and scale up your  organism in a p