ations beyond  health care such as an energy  agriculture bioremediation and chemicals  innumerable products from clothing to  plastics to perfumes are all made with  petroleum derived chemicals or with  specialty chemicals that have  environmentally destructive  ramifications such as palm oil companies  like ich / are using modified strange of  algae to produce palm oil which will  help reduce pressure on the rainforests  in Indonesia and elsewhere ginkgo bio  works is working with traditional  perfumers to design a cultured rose  extract based on numerous molecular  attributes that control for fragrance  other companies such as Jeanine core are  working to create a bio isoprene monomer  which will produce high quality  synthetic rubber without dependence on  petroleum based materials that cause  adverse environmental consequences due  to their high price volume ratio  renewable chemicals are likely to see a  large share of the near-term commercial  activity in engineering biology today  you're seeing price competitive products  derived from sustainable sin bio  chemicals in creams flavors soups and  fragrances applications in  bioremediation are a topic of popular  interest as organisms can be used to  clean up oil spills or consume  environmental contaminants such as  plastic modular genetics in partnership  with several academic universities  engineered a microorganism that produced  soy-based bio dispersants for oil  pollution management which could be used  to assist cleaning up environmental  disasters like the 2010 Deepwater  Horizon  oil spill in the Gulf rather than using  oils from trees grown in the rainforest  some scientists are also chasing the  idea of reintroducing extinct species as  a long-term project by reengineering  nearby relatives or by cloning replacing  the embryonic DNA of a nearby relative  with the DNA of the extinct species like  in Jurassic Park fiction turns into  reality as long as you have the DNA the  sequence DNA for an extinct s